s.tsx:141:21">Data-driven approach without relying on guesswork</span></li><li class="flex gap-3" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:136:19"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-primary" aria-hidden="true" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:137:21"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span class="text-foreground/90" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:141:21">Focus on sustainable, long-term search visibility</span></li><li class="flex gap-3" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:136:19"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-primary" aria-hidden="true" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:137:21"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg><span class="text-foreground/90" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:141:21">Fully aligned with modern Answer Engine and AI search requirements</span></li></ul></div></div></section><section id="introduction" class="scroll-mt-28" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:254:9"><h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-bold lg:text-3xl" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:255:11">What full-stack web development means</h2><div class="space-y-6" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:121:5"><p class="text-balance-pretty text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/90" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:125:13">A full-stack project is one where the same team is responsible for the interface, the server-side logic, the data layer and the connections between them. The frontend handles what people see and interact with. The backend applies business rules, validates input and talks to other systems. The database stores the information, and APIs move data between the parts.</p><p class="text-balance-pretty text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/90" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:125:13">Most business websites do not need this. A content site with pages, a blog and a contact form is usually better served by WordPress. Custom development becomes the right answer when the site has to do something specific to your business — user accounts, calculations, internal workflows, or a connection to software you already run.</p><div class="rounded-xl border-l-4 border-amber bg-amber/10 p-5" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:240:11"><p class="font-display font-semibold" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:241:13">Stack chosen per project</p><p class="mt-1 text-foreground/90" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:242:13">We do not use every technology on every project. The stack is selected around requirements, timeline, hosting and who will maintain the result afterwards.</p></div></div></section><section id="technology-stack" class="scroll-mt-28" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:254:9"><h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-bold lg:text-3xl" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:255:11">Technology stack we work with</h2><div class="space-y-6" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:121:5"><div data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:170:13"><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:172:15"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:173:17"><thead class="bg-mist" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:174:19"><tr data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.tsx:175:21"><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold" data-tsd-source="/src/components/site/sections.ts